<para/><item>Write a rule that describes what the function does. Compare with your group. 💬</item>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> </para>
</list>


<title>Activity Synthesis</title>
<para>The use of multiple inputs allows students to see that the function behaves consistently, and the simulation mimics building an input/output table. The use of the “see-inside” boxes equate to the use of process columns when building tables. 
  </para>

</list>

</section>
